 3. [AND] Being able to communicate in Mandarin [AND] Taiwan.
 4. [AND] Ages over 20 years old.
Exclusion Criteria:
 1. [AND] Cognitive impairment: The MMSE of the above-mentioned educators was 26 points, [AND] the national minimum was < 21 points, those who are [NOT] not educated are <16 points, [AND] the case is excluded.
 2. Patients who have received [NOT] non-emergency dialysis treatment.
 3. Patients with severe cardiopulmonary dysfunction, severe shock, low blood pressure, [OR] large bleeding are [NOT] not controlled.
 4. Patients with chronic active hepatitis, cirrhosis [OR] liver failure.
 5. A history of cancer that may be transferred.
 6. Severe bleeding tendency.
 7. Loss of peritoneal function [OR] extensive peritoneal adhesion, [NOT] unable to use peritoneal dialysis.
 8. [NOT] Unable to correct physiological defects, may interfere with peritoneal dialysis, [OR] increase the chance of infection, such as umbilical hernia.
 9. The patient is [NOT] unable to operate the fluid change, hand shake, [AND] no family members can assist.
 10. Patients who are blind, have poor eyesight, [AND] have difficulty operating.
